    Annotation {
      Name		      "This model was configured to run on the dsPICDEM 2 \ndemo board from Microchip using the  dsPIC30F4011. \n\nIt uses single precision and the control loops run at 10 kHZ \nwith OC1 PWM set at  5 kHZ. "
      Position		      [704, 103]
      BackgroundColor	      "green"
      DropShadow	      on
      FontSize		      20
    }
    Annotation {
      Name		      "Scaling\n\nThe external analogue tachometer can measure +- 250 rad/sec peak. The external hardware scales and offsets the +- peak tacho voltage to  0-5v. You must do same. The internal speed control loop is scaled to run at 150rad/sec to allow for overshoot\n\nThe external LEM Module can measure +- 25 amps peak. The external hardware scales and offsets the LEM voltage from +_ 10V to 0-5v You must do same. The internal control limit is set to +- 15 amps to allow for overshoot..\n\nNote that this model requires all input signals to be POSITIVE. The DC voltage is 128 volts. Change this to your desired output DC voltage.\n\nGOOD LUCK IT SHOULD WORK IF ALL THE FEEDBACK IS CORRECT.\n\nIf you remove just the SIMULINK CNTROLLER you will be able to use the controllers in SIMULINK.  "
      Position		      [792, 808]
      BackgroundColor	      "[1.000000, 1.000000, 0.000000]"
      DropShadow	      on
      FontName		      "Arial Narrow"
      FontSize		      14
    }
